// Ollama cloud web search REST (ollama.com/api/web_search): the `ollama`
// provider of the web_search chain.
//
// Search only. This is Ollama's hosted search API on ollama.com, not a local
// Ollama server; no model runs and Ollama's chat and generate endpoints are
// never declared. The search endpoint returns result links, so this provider
// is built.
//
// Wire contract pinned from Ollama's own documentation and its own client
// (read 2026-10-20):
// - the web search capability page,
//   https://docs.ollama.com/capabilities/web-search ("Authentication", "Web
//   search API": request, response and the cURL example);
// - the API introduction, https://docs.ollama.com/api (cloud base URL
//   https://ollama.com/api; "Cloud requests need an API key", supplied in the
//   `Authorization: Bearer` header);
// - the error page, https://docs.ollama.com/api/errors (statuses and the
//   {"error": "..."} JSON body);
// - Ollama's official Python client, https://github.com/ollama/ollama-python:
//   ollama/_client.py (web_search posts to the fixed URL
//   https://ollama.com/api/web_search and requires an
//   "Authorization: Bearer ..." header) and ollama/_types.py
//   (WebSearchRequest: query, max_results; WebSearchResponse: results of
//   WebSearchResult with content, title and url).
//
// - method and path: POST https://ollama.com/api/web_search with a JSON body.
//   The transport URL is the host and the path carries /api/web_search;
// - auth: `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, an API key created at
//   https://ollama.com/settings/keys (OLLAMA_API_KEY in Ollama's examples). The
//   connection is bound to the vault credential `apikey:ollama-cloud`; plexus
//   reads it by name at dispatch and never stores it;
// - request fields used: `query` (string, required; no length limit
//   documented) and `max_results` (integer, optional, "default 5, max 10"; no
//   minimum documented, so the schema takes 1 to 10). Nothing else is
//   documented and nothing else is sent. No domain filter, no date filter and
//   no query operator is documented;
// - reply: {results: [...]}, each with `title`, `url` and `content` (the
//   documented "relevant content snippet"). All three are read; nothing else
//   is documented. The Python client types each as optional;
// - errors (error page, for the whole API): 400 Bad Request, 404 Not Found,
//   429 Too Many Requests ("e.g. when rate limit exceeded"), 500 Internal
//   Server Error and 502 Bad Gateway, with an {"error": "..."} body. 401 and
//   403 are not on that page; Ollama's cloud usage reference documents them
//   for its own endpoint (GET /api/usage) as invalid credentials and a
//   suspended account, and they are read the same way here. No 402, no quota
//   status, no Retry-After and no rate figure is documented for web search.
//
// Differences from the provider facts the web_search chain design started from
// (POST https://ollama.com/api/web_search; bearer; query and max_results, max
// 10; site: in query; results[].title, url, content):
// - credential: the vault record is `apikey:ollama-cloud`, not
//   `apikey:ollama`. This is the vault name agreed with the vault's owners and
//   already recorded in the web_search provider table; the key is an
//   ollama.com account key, which a local Ollama server does not use;
// - domains: the design's row says `site:` in the query, but Ollama documents
//   no `site:` operator (or any other operator) and no domain field. An
//   operator Ollama might silently ignore would return unfiltered results as
//   if they were filtered, so plexus treats domains as unsupported: a search
//   that asks for any domain skips Ollama for capability and the chain moves
//   on. The query is sent exactly as the caller wrote it;
// - recency: none is documented, so a search with a recency window skips
//   Ollama for capability instead of being answered with results of any age;
// - query length: none is documented, so the tool's own 500-character limit
//   applies to the query as sent;
// - dates: the reply carries no date, so no result reports a publication date;
// - outcome classification: 400 is a rejected request; 401 is a credential
//   failure; 429 is throttled for 60 seconds, or for its Retry-After if one is
//   sent; 403, 404, 500 and 502 are unavailable for 60 seconds. Ollama
//   documents no status for a used-up plan, so no reply is classified as
//   quota unless it is a 402 or its body names credits or quota.
//
// The search action is read-risk and has no side effects, so a retry is safe.
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "key": "ollama_rest",
  "name": "Ollama Web Search (REST)",
  "description": "Web search over Ollama's cloud web search API (ollama.com/api/web_search), as a provider for web_search.",
  "reuse_path": "openapi_shim",
  "reuse_rationale": "Small JSON REST API with static API-key bearer auth, used by Ollama's own clients; a search mutates no vendor-side state, so it maps to a read grant.",
  "tier": "S1",
  "transport": {
    "kind": "rest_api",
    "url": "https://ollama.com"
  },
  "auth": {
    "mode": "api_key"
  },
  "credential_bindings": [
    {
      "ref_role": "api_key",
      "placement": "header",
      "key": "Authorization",
      "prefix": "Bearer ",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "resource_filters": {
    "required": [],
    "optional": [],
    "write_enabling": []
  },
  "actions_baseline": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "risk": "read",
      "http": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/web_search",
        "args_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "query": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 500 },
            "max_results": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 10 }
          },
          "required": ["query"],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "ask_first_risk": ["write", "destructive"],
    "rate_limit": { "calls_per_min": 30 }
  },
  "availability": "ga"
}
